    "text": "Projects / Reproducible AI agent algorithm benchmark Packing Arena A reproducible one-dimensional bin-packing tournament where three independent AI coding agents ( Scarlet , Cobalt , and Jade ) implement deterministic solvers, perform circular code review with concrete counterexamples, revise once, and compete on a pre-committed 108-case synthetic benchmark. Live Results Explorer Source on GitHub Release v0.1.0 All projects Period October 2026 Release v0.1.0 Work type Independent project Development AI-assisted, with verification Overview Evidence Scope 01 / Overview What I built A zero-dependency Python benchmarking harness and interactive static results explorer designed to test multi-agent algorithm design, adversarial code critique, and strict verification gates on 1D bin packing (capacity 100 , 0–180 items per case): Sealed Pre-Committed Dataset ( cases.json ) : 108 synthetic instances across 8 families ( edge , uniform , small , large , near_third , complements , mixed , and 24 exact_small cases with proven optima), locked by SHA-256 ( ffa9821b... ) before any peer review or revision. Three Deterministic Solvers & Circular Peer Review : Each agent combined Best-Fit Decreasing (BFD), bitset subset-sum completion, L2/cardinality lower bounds, and operation-budgeted exact search. In the review round, Scarlet constructed a 60-triple counterexample where Cobalt used 61 bins; Cobalt identified an early depth >= 600 cutoff in Jade (57 vs. 55 bins); and Jade exposed missing cardinality lower bounds in Scarlet . Deterministic Judge & Independent Oracle ( judge.py , verify.py ) : Evaluates 1,944 total calls (108 cases × 3 agents × 2 rounds × 3 rotated repetitions), checking index completeness, bin capacity, non-mutation of input arrays, output determinism across repetitions, and agreement with an exhaustive branch-and-bound oracle cross-checked on 60 random cases. Interactive Results Dashboard ( index.html ) : Dependency-free browser explorer comparing pre-review (`round1/`) and post-review packings, family-level bin totals against the 3,333-bin BFD baseline, per-bin visual item bars, full peer-review transcripts, and frozen source code. Python 3.10–3.14 Combinatorial Optimization Bitset DP & Branch-and-Bound Multi-Agent Peer Review GitHub Pages 02 / Evidence What was checked Published Packing Arena scoreboard on GitHub Pages comparing final vs. initial snapshots, family breakdowns, and visual bin contents. Release audit: 26 October 2026 (commit e417e3f1 , release v0.1.0 ). Both Jade ( 0.135 ms median) and Scarlet ( 0.251 ms median) reduced total bins from the 3,333 BFD baseline to 3,321 with zero failures and 29/29 exact-small optimum hits. Cobalt achieved the same 3,321 output bins but exceeded the 1-second limit on case C017 ( 1,632.29 ms ) after stacking pattern search ahead of unbucketed list operations. Verified by 4 unittest suites and 648 saved-packing checks on Linux CI (Python 3.10 & 3.14) and Windows. Live GitHub Pages demo Repository source Release v0.1.0 Verified CI run 03 / Scope What this demonstrates Reproducible benchmarking, pre-committed dataset hashing, independent oracle verification, and transparent reporting of both improvements and regressions (such as Cobalt's post-revision timeout). All test cases are synthetic, and the three contestants are sub-agents of the same parent model rather than separate model families. Wall-clock tie-breaker measurements reflect the recorded Windows run; CI verifies algorithmic correctness and frozen evidence hashes. All projects"
