    "title": "ApplyProof",
    "url": "https://ardhyanovri.my.id/projects/applyproof.html",
    "category": "Project",
    "text": "Projects / Evidence-based applications ApplyProof Job-application drafts where every sentence traces back to a reviewed fact. View repository All projects Type Open-source tool Focus Job applications AI use Optional, fact-ID based Repo vanovri/applyproof On this page Problem Approach Build gallery Results Lessons 01 / Problem Problem Application drafts drift away from what a person can actually prove. I wanted every sentence to trace back to a reviewed fact. 02 / Approach Approach Fact ledger Reviewed, evidence-based Skill comparison Explicit match to a role Office vs worksite Distinguished Drafts Traceable, verbatim facts 03 / Build gallery Build gallery The public ApplyProof repository. 04 / Results Results No invented claims: drafts are assembled only from reviewed facts, and the optional AI returns fact IDs, never prose. Gaps made visible before drafting: explicit skill coverage separates exposure from hands-on skill, and unresolved requirements are listed. Location assumptions caught: an office address alone leaves the worksite unverified. Traceable, reproducible exports: Markdown/JSON output carries fact IDs, source excerpts and an evidence digest. 05 / Lessons Lessons Letting AI pick fact IDs, not write claims, keeps drafts honest. ← Previous RepairGate Next → IoT Temperature Monitoring & DC Motor Control"
