    "title": "DataRescue",
    "url": "https://ardhyanovri.my.id/projects/datarescue.html",
    "category": "Project",
    "text": "Projects / Data validation workbench DataRescue Repair messy CSV/JSON without losing track of a single row. View repository All projects Type Open-source tool Interface Workbench + CLI Data CSV / JSON Repo vanovri/datarescue On this page Problem Approach Build gallery Results Lessons 01 / Problem Problem Messy CSV and JSON files need validating and repairing before they are useful, and every change should be traceable. 02 / Approach Approach Input CSV / JSON files Rules Rule-based normalization Quarantine Rejected rows set aside Audit Report exports 03 / Build gallery Build gallery The public DataRescue repository. 04 / Results Results Fewer manual validation errors: rule-based validation and normalization replace hand-checking of CSV/JSON rows. Nothing silently lost: rejected rows are quarantined instead of dropped, so every repair can be reviewed and reversed. Traceable changes: exported audit reports record what was changed and what was rejected. Reproducible pipeline: the same rules run from the local workbench or the CLI, and behaviour is covered by automated tests (AI-assisted). 05 / Lessons Lessons Keeping rejected rows instead of dropping them makes repairs auditable. ← Previous uart-fixture-kit Next → RepairGate"
